307 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 104 0 R
/T (The pointer and struct designs give the same answer \(3 eligible donors; youngest eligible is 104, age 22; donor 102 is under 18 and 103 donated only 50 days ago\). The lowest stock is 5 units at index 6.)
/E (The pointer and struct designs give the same answer \(3 eligible donors; youngest eligible is 104, age 22; donor 102 is under 18 and 103 donated only 50 days ago\). The lowest stock is 5 units at index 6.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
308 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 104 0 R
/T (Index instead of pointer: if find_lowest returned an index, the caller would write stock[i] += 50. Time O\(n\) and space O\(1\) in both versions. The index stays valid if the array is later reallocated; a stored pointer would dangle, so the index version is safer, while the pointer version is more convenient to use.)
/E (Index instead of pointer: if find_lowest returned an index, the caller would write stock[i] += 50. Time O\(n\) and space O\(1\) in both versions. The index stays valid if the array is later reallocated; a stored pointer would dangle, so the index version is safer, while the pointer version is more convenient to use.)
/Pg 14 0 R
