514 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 107 0 R
/T (Changing half * half to two calls gives 63 calls for n = 30 instead of 6, and 32,767 calls for n = 10,000. The same sub-problem is solved twice at every level, so T\(n\) = 2T\(n/2\) + 1 = O\(n\) and the speed advantage of halving is lost. Recursion limit: the linear version crashed between n = 261,742 and 262,505 on this machine. With an 8 MB stack and about 32 bytes per frame, 8,388,608 / 32 = 262,144 frames, which agrees. The crash is a stack overflow \(segmentation fault\). The iterative version handled n = 1,000,000,000 using constant stack. The limit depends on the machine and stack size, so rerun stack_limit on your own computer.)
/E (Changing half * half to two calls gives 63 calls for n = 30 instead of 6, and 32,767 calls for n = 10,000. The same sub-problem is solved twice at every level, so T\(n\) = 2T\(n/2\) + 1 = O\(n\) and the speed advantage of halving is lost. Recursion limit: the linear version crashed between n = 261,742 and 262,505 on this machine. With an 8 MB stack and about 32 bytes per frame, 8,388,608 / 32 = 262,144 frames, which agrees. The crash is a stack overflow \(segmentation fault\). The iterative version handled n = 1,000,000,000 using constant stack. The limit depends on the machine and stack size, so rerun stack_limit on your own computer.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [79]
>>
endobj
