/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 108 0 R
/T (If realloc\(\) fails it returns NULL and leaves the old block untouched, so the function returns 0, the existing donors are still safe and the caller can save them and report the error. If the result were assigned directly to list->data, a failure would overwrite the only pointer with NULL: all donors would be lost and the old block leaked \(this is why the temporary pointer p is used\).)
/E (If realloc\(\) fails it returns NULL and leaves the old block untouched, so the function returns 0, the existing donors are still safe and the caller can save them and report the error. If the result were assigned directly to list->data, a failure would overwrite the only pointer with NULL: all donors would be lost and the old block leaked \(this is why the temporary pointer p is used\).)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
