/S /H2
/P 111 0 R
/T (The capacity sequence 2, 2, 4, 4, 8 matches the expected output. For 5,000,000 donors the list capacity grows to 8,388,608 x 16 bytes = 128 MB \(peak resident memory 77.9 MB because unused pages are not touched\). Both modes find the same number of eligible donors.)
/E (The capacity sequence 2, 2, 4, 4, 8 matches the expected output. For 5,000,000 donors the list capacity grows to 8,388,608 x 16 bytes = 128 MB \(peak resident memory 77.9 MB because unused pages are not touched\). Both modes find the same number of eligible donors.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [44]
>>
endobj
702 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 111 0 R
/T (Why a temporary pointer p: if realloc fails and its result is stored directly in list->data, the old pointer is lost \(memory leak and lost data\). With p, the old block stays usable on failure.)
