/Title (Alternative: getline\(\) instead of fgets. getline allocates a buffer of the needed size, so no input is truncated. Time to read a line of length L is O\(L\) \(plus occasional buffer growth\) and the heap space is O\(L\) instead of a fixed array. The caller must free the buffer. A maximum length should still be checked so that a huge line cannot use all memory.)
