1981 0 obj
<<
/Title (Engineering trade-off. Binary files are not always portable: another computer or compiler may use a different int size, byte order \(endianness\) or structure padding, so the same bytes can be read wrongly. Text is portable and human-readable but slower and not updatable in place. Recommendation: use a text \(CSV-style\) file for donors \(variable length, shared between hospitals, easy to check\) and a fixed-record binary file for stock \(numbers only, small, updated very often\).)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1949 0 R
/Prev 1971 0 R
/Next 1972 0 R
>>
endobj
