/Title (Production decision \(B4.3\). For a nightly report \(one pass over the data\) the batch method is the better choice: it took almost the same time as loading everything \(627 ms vs 671 ms for 5 million donors\) but needed 0.15 MB instead of up to 128 MB. For interactive searches \(find by group, update\) the donors of one hospital \(about 1 MB for 50,000 donors\) can simply be kept in the growable list. If a single donor must be looked up by ID without loading everything, a separate sorted index file with fseek and binary search needs O\(1\) memory and O\(log n\) file reads \(about 23 reads for 5 million donors\) per lookup, compared with O\(1\) lookup but O\(n\) memory after loading.)
